        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Places: Menindee Lakes, Menindee, New South Wales, Australia, Central Darling Shire, Darling River\n- Topics: location, population, spelling\n\nFacts:\n- Menindee Lakes lie in the far west region of New South Wales, Australia, near the town of Menindee.\n- Menindee is a small town in the far west of New South Wales, Australia, in Central Darling Shire, on the banks of the Darling River.\n- Menindee is frequently but erroneously spelled \"Menindie\".\n- Menindee had a sign-posted population of 980.\n- In the 2011 census, Menindee had a population of 449.",
